---
description: |
  Normalizes a Cloudflare Logpush record to OCSF.

  ```tql
  from_file "s3://example-logpush/http_requests/**/*.log.gz" {
    decompress_gzip
    read_ndjson
  }
  cloudflare::ocsf::normalize
  ```

  Logpush delivers newline-delimited JSON, which Tenzir reads natively, so the
  package starts at the mapper. The operator maps HTTP requests and firewall
  events to OCSF HTTP Activity and audit logs to OCSF API Activity. Whatever
  has no OCSF attribute remains under `unmapped`.

  Callers who already hold a structured Logpush record under another field, or
  who want to inspect and enrich the record before mapping, use
  `cloudflare::ocsf::map`.
args:
  positional:
    - name: cloudflare
      description: The structured Cloudflare Logpush record.
      type: field
      default: this
  named:
    - name: dataset
      type: string
      default: null
      description: |
        The Logpush dataset of the record: `http_requests`, `firewall_events`,
        or `audit_logs_v2`. Defaults to recognizing the dataset by its fields.
    - name: into
      description: The field that receives the OCSF event.
      type: field
      default: this
---

$into.cloudflare = $cloudflare
cloudflare::ocsf::map $into.cloudflare, $into.ocsf, dataset=$dataset
$into = $into.ocsf
